{"schema_version":"1.0.0","id":"cik-0001805077","cik":"0001805077","slug":"eos-energy-enterprises-805077","name":"Eos Energy Enterprises, Inc.","ticker":"EOSE","exchanges":["Nasdaq","Nasdaq"],"sector":"Miscellaneous Electrical Machinery, Equipment & Supplies","sic":"3690","country":"PA","website":"","listed_years":5.4,"first_annual":"2021-02-26","last_filing":"2026-07-28","annual_only":false,"edgar_url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0001805077&type=10-K","summary":{"sentences":["Eos Energy Enterprises, Inc. files with the SEC under \"Miscellaneous Electrical Machinery, Equipment & Supplies\", based in PA, and has been publicly reporting for 5 years.","It reported $113.2m of revenue over the trailing four quarters, up 444.7% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of -78.0%.","Listed on Nasdaq, Nasdaq, it is still consuming cash, with roughly 22 months of runway at the current burn."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Revenue grew 444.7% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025), reaching $57.0m in the quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1805077/000162828026034368/0001628280-26-034368-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-034368"},{"text":"Growth has been positive in 6 of the last 8 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1805077/000162828026034368/0001628280-26-034368-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-034368"},{"text":"Gross margin expanded from -234.7% to -78.0% against the same quarter a year earlier - the company is keeping more of what it sells, not buying growth with discounts.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1805077/000162828026034368/0001628280-26-034368-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-034368"}],"bear":[{"text":"Growth is erratic - a standard deviation of 1159.9% across 8 comparisons. Lumpy revenue usually means few customers or long contracts, and both make any single quarter a poor guide.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1805077/000162828026034368/0001628280-26-034368-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-034368"},{"text":"Gross margin is only -78.0%, so scale has to be enormous before anything reaches the bottom line.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1805077/000162828026034368/0001628280-26-034368-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-034368"},{"text":"The company is loss-making at the operating line (-139.2% margin). Profitability is a forecast, not a fact.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1805077/000162828026034368/0001628280-26-034368-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-034368"},{"text":"The operating loss widened by $26.4m against the same quarter a year earlier - it is getting worse, not better.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1805077/000162828026034368/0001628280-26-034368-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-034368"},{"text":"About 22 months of cash at the current burn ($410.7m against $219.6m a year). A company that must raise is a company that raises on the buyer's terms.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1805077/000162828026034368/0001628280-26-034368-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-034368"},{"text":"Diluted share count rose 24.9% over the year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). The company can grow while your share of it shrinks, and this is the number most commentary ignores.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1805077/000162828026034368/0001628280-26-034368-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-034368"},{"text":"Shareholders' equity is negative (-$868.4m) - liabilities exceed assets on the balance sheet.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1805077/000162828026034368/0001628280-26-034368-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-034368"},{"text":"Insiders disposed of 11.4% of their combined holdings over the last four quarters (398,339 shares across 14 ownership filings). People with the best view of the business were reducing their stake.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1805077/000162828026050230/0001628280-26-050230-index.htm"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 0.6% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1805077/000162828026050230/0001628280-26-050230-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 0.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.0,"consecutive":2,"current":-0.78,"current_display":"-78.0%","threshold_display":"0.0%","fired":true,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below 222.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":2.22,"consecutive":2,"current":4.447,"current_display":"444.7%","threshold_display":"222.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"runway_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Cash runway falls below 12 months","metric":"runway_months","comparison":"below","threshold":12.0,"consecutive":1,"current":22.439,"current_display":"22 months","threshold_display":"12 months","fired":false,"ra